# Next.js Best Practices

## Server-First Architecture

- Prefer React Server Components (RSC) over client components whenever possible
- Use "use client" directive only when absolutely necessary (interactivity, browser APIs, event handlers)
- Keep client-side JavaScript minimal and focused on user interactions
- Fetch data directly in server components using the Data Access Layer (DAL)
- Use server actions for all data mutations, never client-side API calls

## State Management

- Store application state in the URL when possible (search params, route params)
- Use React's built-in state management for component-specific state
- Avoid unnecessary global state - prefer URL state and server state
- Use React Context sparingly, only for theme and authentication state

## Data Access Patterns

- All DAL functions should handle user authentication internally
- Server components should call DAL methods directly for data fetching
- Server actions should call DAL methods for data mutations
- DAL methods should throw UnauthorizedError if user lacks permissions
- Use tryCatch from @walkup/walkup-utils for consistent error handling

## Routing and Layout

- Use the App Router architecture
- Implement nested layouts appropriately
- Optimize loading states and error boundaries
- Use dynamic imports for code splitting
- Implement proper metadata for SEO

## Performance

- Optimize images with next/image
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Implement incremental static regeneration where appropriate
- Optimize third-party script loading
- Implement incremental static regeneration where appropriate
- Optimize third-party script loading
